25:Tb94,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use Nearby Restaurants","description":"Hungry in a new neighbourhood? This nearby restaurants tool finds restaurants, cafés and eateries around any area in India or around your current location, with addresses and map links. Use it to find a place close to your hotel, office or event, and to explore local food beyond the places you alrea","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/nearby-restaurants","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"Nearby Restaurants"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to find restaurants near you","text":"Type a locality or use your location, select the radius and search. The list shows nearby restaurants with their addresses. Open the map link to check the distance and the route, and then call or check the menu on the restaurant’s own page."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Choosing a good place to eat","text":"Look for places with a steady stream of local customers, a short menu that is clearly done well and visible hygiene in the serving area. Ratings help, but read the recent reviews to see whether quality has changed."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Food safety and hygiene basics","text":"Choose freshly cooked and hot food, drink sealed or filtered water and be cautious with raw salads and cut fruit in extreme heat. Restaurants must display a valid FSSAI licence or registration, and you can check the number with our FSSAI tool before you trust a packaged or takeaway brand."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Finding the right kind of restaurant","text":"India’s eating-out options range from street stalls and dhabas to cafés, family restaurants, fine dining and regional specialities. The right choice depends on the occasion. For a quick meal, look for a busy place with a short menu. For a family dinner, check seating, parking and whether the restaurant takes reservations. For a business lunch, pick a quieter spot close to the meeting location."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Eating out with dietary needs","text":"If you follow a vegetarian, Jain, vegan or halal diet, or have an allergy, do not rely on the name of a place alone. Call ahead and ask how food is prepared, whether the kitchen is separate, and which oils or ingredients are used. In India, a green dot marks vegetarian items and a brown dot marks non-vegetarian ones on packaged foods, and many restaurants follow the same practice on menus."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"Ordering, paying and tipping","text":"Most restaurants accept UPI, cards and cash, but small eateries and dhabas may take only cash or UPI. Check that the bill lists GST correctly; a service charge is optional unless it was clearly printed on the menu before you ordered, and you can ask for it to be removed if it was not. A tip of around 5 to 10 per cent is common if you were happy with the service."}]}23:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$25"}}]
