2e:["$","div","Finding the right kind of restaurant",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Finding the right kind of restaurant"}],[["$","p","India’s eating-out options range from street sta",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"India’s eating-out options range from street stalls and dhabas to cafés, family restaurants, fine dining and regional specialities. The right choice depends on the occasion. For a quick meal, look for a busy place with a short menu. For a family dinner, check seating, parking and whether the restaurant takes reservations. For a business lunch, pick a quieter spot close to the meeting location."}],["$","p","When you travel, search for local specialities r",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"When you travel, search for local specialities rather than only familiar chains. A thali place in Gujarat, a dosa restaurant in Chennai, a fish-curry kitchen in Goa or a kebab lane in Lucknow will usually give a better meal than a generic menu. Search by area, scan the names on the list and then use the map link to see how far each one is."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Family dinner: check seating, parking and booking",{"children":"Family dinner: check seating, parking and booking"}],["$","li","Quick meal: choose a busy, short-menu place close by",{"children":"Quick meal: choose a busy, short-menu place close by"}],["$","li","Travel: look for regional specialities over chains",{"children":"Travel: look for regional specialities over chains"}]]}],null]}]
